PARSFILE
#FullDataName Generic VS Commands`Simulation Time Controls`Miscellaneous Custom Controls
#VehCode Simulation Output Controls

#MiscYellow0
! do not decimate the results - to avoid distorting the clutch control waveforms
iprint 0

! define new parameters to control simulation write status
define_parameter write_on = 1; units = -; Setting opt_write to write_on will enable writing to disk.
define_parameter write_off = 0; units = -; Setting opt_write to write_off will disable writing to disk.

define_parameter write_start = 2; units = s; Begin recording output at this time
define_parameter write_end = 3; units = s; Finish recording output at this time

! Use an EQ statement to control the value of opt_write every time step
EQ_IN opt_write = IF( ( T >= write_start ) & ( T <= write_end ), write_on, write_off)
#ENDMYellow

*MODELCODE Simulation Output Controls

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset controls when the results are written to disk.  Only a brief time period in the results is kept, this is to make the specific shift behavior of interest more visible on the plots.
#
#To view the entire simulation output, just unlink this dataset and run the simulation again.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Generic VS Commands; { Miscellaneous Custom Controls } Simulation Time Controls
#Library : Generic VS Commands
#DataSet : Simulation Time Controls
#Category: Miscellaneous Custom Controls
